* LTC6252 High-Speed Amplifier Configured for a Gain of 2 V/V
* Supplies: +/-5V
* Input: 1V amplitude sine wave at 10 MHz

* Power Supplies
VCC VCC 0 5
VEE VEE 0 -5

* Input Signal (1V peak, 10 MHz)
VIN IN 0 SINE(0 1 10Meg)

* Feedback Network for Non-Inverting Gain of 2
* Using 402 ohms, a standard value for high-speed op-amps to minimize parasitic pole effects
R1 IN_MINUS 0 402
R2 OUT IN_MINUS 402

* LTC6252 Subcircuit Instantiation
* Pinout: IN+ IN- V+ V- OUT SHDN
* SHDN is tied to VCC to enable the amplifier
X1 IN IN_MINUS VCC VEE OUT VCC LTC6252

* Transient Analysis
* Run for 2us, start saving data at 1us to ensure steady-state settled output
.tran 0 2u 1u

* Measurements to calculate Gain in dB
.measure tran out_pp PP V(OUT)
.measure tran in_pp PP V(IN)
.measure tran gain_db param 20*log10(out_pp/in_pp)

* Include the standard LTspice library containing the LTC6252
.lib LTC6.lib

.end
